{"id":"73b1b81d-0b03-40cd-939d-7a606c99653f","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"03c26f36278bcf49","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/type-queries/extension.ts","baseline":{"blob":"b3823d05b7c245c23a7dd7b1e1b5a3adfed35e75","start":3593,"end":3642},"shape":{"type":"If","atoms":["if","(","queries",".","length","===","0",")","{","return","[","]",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"26c18370d4925a39","after":"3a06974fe09f18d7"}},"payload":{"text":"(asked of every file as it's shown and edited: a span only when there are queries to answer)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:55.005Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:55.005Z"}
{"id":"8a32a806-dc27-4546-af45-e4faa67cf9da","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"31c18815db9b5175","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/type-queries/extension.ts","baseline":{"blob":"57fd733b1b10ca2895c8edfa9a2160be15851dc9","start":0,"end":69},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","{","observeExtension","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/editor-api/runtime","\""]},"context":{"after":"f2517b5f32f25ee8"}},"payload":{"text":"Type Queries — `// ^?` beneath an expression shows its type, as in the TypeScript Playground and twoslash:\n\nconst message = greet(\"world\")\n//    ^? const message: string\n\nThe caret points at a column of the line above (past any other query lines stacked there); what hovering that\ncharacter would say — TypeScript's quick info, the code block of its hover — is an inlay hint after the `^?`. Public\nAPI only (an inlay-hints provider asking the hover providers), so it works the same in a desktop VS Code.\n\nA query's answer can change when another file does (the function it calls), and inlay hints are only re-asked for\non an edit to their own document; diagnostics changing is the sign TypeScript has re-checked, so that re-asks too.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:59.947Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:59.947Z"}
{"id":"9c8b4072-3521-4462-8786-6c8264aaa51a","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"752f529242fc4385","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/type-queries/extension.ts","baseline":{"blob":"8b2479ac264b857dd3d2da131f75cf94b02982b4","start":1012,"end":1093},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","QUICK_INFO","=","/","```(?:typescript|ts|tsx|javascript|js|jsx)\\n([\\s\\S]*?)\\n```","/","u"]},"context":{"before":"60d3d769da8ebc6f","after":"6c4bef9fb9bb020d"}},"payload":{"text":"TypeScript's hover leads with its quick info as a fenced code block.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:58.943Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:58.943Z"}
{"id":"ba7072f4-a3f7-4319-acd3-16d31ea1eac4","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"6c4bef9fb9bb020d","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/type-queries/extension.ts","baseline":{"blob":"0326d8b15664988f69edae37bf8f67cef30ee20f","start":1167,"end":1188},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","MAX_LABEL","=","120"]},"context":{"before":"752f529242fc4385","after":"f3c1ca0740742530"}},"payload":{"text":"One line in the editor; the full answer is the hint's tooltip.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:57.045Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:57.045Z"}
